Task 1: Set Up Provisioning Templates
Subtask 1.1: Configure Kickstart Templates
Kickstart templates automate the installation process for RHEL systems.

Step 1: Access Satellite Web Interface
Open your web browser and navigate to the Satellite server
Log in with administrator credentials
# Access Satellite web interface
https://satellite.example.com
Username: admin
Password: [provided-password]
Step 2: Create Custom Kickstart Template
Navigate to Hosts → Templates → Provisioning Templates
Click Create Template
Select Kickstart as the template type
<%#
kind: provision
name: Custom RHEL Kickstart
model: ProvisioningTemplate
oses:
- RedHat Enterprise Linux 8
- RedHat Enterprise Linux 9
%>

# Custom Kickstart Template for RHEL
install
url --url="<%= @medium_uri %>"
lang en_US.UTF-8
keyboard us
timezone America/New_York --isUtc

# Network configuration
network --bootproto=dhcp --device=<%= @host.mac %> --hostname=<%= @host.name %>

# Root password (will be set during provisioning)
rootpw --iscrypted <%= root_pass %>

# Firewall configuration
firewall --enabled --ssh

# SELinux configuration
selinux --enforcing

# Disk partitioning
zerombr
clearpart --all --initlabel
autopart --type=lvm

# Package selection
%packages --ignoremissing
@core
@base
openssh-server
wget
curl
vim
%end

# Post-installation script
%post --log=/root/ks-post.log
# Register with Satellite
curl -o /tmp/bootstrap.py <%= foreman_url('built') %>
python3 /tmp/bootstrap.py

# Enable and start SSH
systemctl enable sshd
systemctl start sshd

# Update system
dnf update -y

# Signal completion
curl -X POST <%= foreman_url('built') %>
%end

reboot
Step 3: Save and Associate Template
Click Submit to save the template
Navigate to Administer → Settings → Provisioning
Set the default Kickstart template for your operating system
Subtask 1.2: Configure PXE Templates
PXE (Preboot Execution Environment) enables network-based booting.

Step 1: Create PXE Default Template
Navigate to Hosts → Templates → Provisioning Templates
Click Create Template
Select PXELinux as template type
# PXE Default Template
DEFAULT menu
PROMPT 0
MENU TITLE Satellite PXE Boot Menu
TIMEOUT 200

LABEL local
  MENU LABEL Boot from local drive
  MENU DEFAULT
  LOCALBOOT 0

LABEL install
  MENU LABEL Install RHEL 8
  KERNEL boot/vmlinuz
  APPEND initrd=boot/initrd.img inst.ks=<%= foreman_url('provision') %> inst.stage2=<%= @medium_uri %>

LABEL rescue
  MENU LABEL Rescue Mode
  KERNEL boot/vmlinuz
  APPEND initrd=boot/initrd.img rescue inst.stage2=<%= @medium_uri %>
Step 2: Configure PXE Discovery
# PXE Discovery Template
DEFAULT menu
PROMPT 0
MENU TITLE Satellite Discovery
TIMEOUT 200

LABEL discovery
  MENU LABEL Discover Host
  MENU DEFAULT
  KERNEL boot/fdi-image/vmlinuz0
  APPEND initrd=boot/fdi-image/initrd0.img rootflags=loop root=live:/fdi.iso rootfstype=auto ro rd.live.image acpi=force rd.luks=0 rd.md=0 rd.dm=0 rd.lvm=0 rd.bootif=0 rd.neednet=0 nomodeset proxy.url=<%= foreman_server_url %> proxy.type=foreman
Subtask 1.3: Configure iPXE Templates
iPXE provides enhanced network booting capabilities.

Step 1: Create iPXE Template
# iPXE Template
#!ipxe

echo Starting iPXE boot for <%= @host.name %>
echo MAC Address: <%= @host.mac %>
echo IP Address: <%= @host.ip %>

# Set network configuration
dhcp

# Boot kernel and initrd
kernel <%= @kernel %> <%= pxe_kernel_options %>
initrd <%= @initrd %>

# Boot the system
boot
Step 2: Configure iPXE Chain Loading
# iPXE Chain Template
#!ipxe

# Chain load based on architecture
cpuid --ext 29 && set arch x86_64 || set arch i386
goto ${arch}

:x86_64
chain <%= foreman_server_url %>/unattended/iPXE?mac=${net0/mac}
goto end

:i386
chain <%= foreman_server_url %>/unattended/iPXE?mac=${net0/mac}
goto end

:end
Task 2: Configure DHCP, DNS, and TFTP Services via Capsule Servers
Subtask 2.1: Configure DHCP Service
Step 1: Install and Configure DHCP on Capsule Server
# Connect to Capsule Server
ssh root@capsule.example.com

# Install DHCP server
dnf install -y dhcp-server

# Configure DHCP
cat > /etc/dhcp/dhcpd.conf << 'EOF'
# DHCP Configuration for Satellite Provisioning
default-lease-time 600;
max-lease-time 7200;
authoritative;

# Subnet configuration
subnet 192.168.1.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {
    range 192.168.1.100 192.168.1.200;
    option routers 192.168.1.1;
    option domain-name-servers 192.168.1.20;
    option domain-name "example.com";
    
    # PXE boot configuration
    next-server 192.168.1.20;
    filename "pxelinux.0";
}

# Host reservations will be managed by Satellite
include "/etc/dhcp/dhcpd.hosts";
EOF

# Create hosts file
touch /etc/dhcp/dhcpd.hosts

# Enable and start DHCP service
systemctl enable dhcpd
systemctl start dhcpd
systemctl status dhcpd
Step 2: Configure Satellite to Manage DHCP
# On Satellite server
satellite-installer --foreman-proxy-dhcp true \
                   --foreman-proxy-dhcp-managed true \
                   --foreman-proxy-dhcp-interface eth0 \
                   --foreman-proxy-dhcp-gateway 192.168.1.1 \
                   --foreman-proxy-dhcp-range "192.168.1.100 192.168.1.200" \
                   --foreman-proxy-dhcp-nameservers "192.168.1.20"
Subtask 2.2: Configure DNS Service
Step 1: Install and Configure DNS on Capsule Server
# Install BIND DNS server
dnf install -y bind bind-utils

# Configure named.conf
cat > /etc/named.conf << 'EOF'
options {
    listen-on port 53 { 127.0.0.1; 192.168.1.20; };
    directory "/var/named";
    dump-file "/var/named/data/cache_dump.db";
    statistics-file "/var/named/data/named_stats.txt";
    memstatistics-file "/var/named/data/named_mem_stats.txt";
    allow-query { localhost; 192.168.1.0/24; };
    recursion yes;
    forwarders { 8.8.8.8; 8.8.4.4; };
};

zone "example.com" IN {
    type master;
    file "example.com.zone";
    allow-update { localhost; };
};

zone "1.168.192.in-addr.arpa" IN {
    type master;
    file "1.168.192.in-addr.arpa.zone";
    allow-update { localhost; };
};
EOF

# Create forward zone file
cat > /var/named/example.com.zone << 'EOF'
$TTL 86400
@   IN  SOA     capsule.example.com. admin.example.com. (
        2023010101  ; Serial
        3600        ; Refresh
        1800        ; Retry
        604800      ; Expire
        86400       ; Minimum TTL
)

@           IN  NS      capsule.example.com.
capsule     IN  A       192.168.1.20
satellite   IN  A       192.168.1.10
EOF

# Create reverse zone file
cat > /var/named/1.168.192.in-addr.arpa.zone << 'EOF'
$TTL 86400
@   IN  SOA     capsule.example.com. admin.example.com. (
        2023010101  ; Serial
        3600        ; Refresh
        1800        ; Retry
        604800      ; Expire
        86400       ; Minimum TTL
)

@       IN  NS      capsule.example.com.
20      IN  PTR     capsule.example.com.
10      IN  PTR     satellite.example.com.
EOF

# Set proper permissions
chown named:named /var/named/*.zone
chmod 644 /var/named/*.zone

# Enable and start DNS service
systemctl enable named
systemctl start named
systemctl status named
Step 2: Configure Satellite to Manage DNS
# Configure DNS integration
satellite-installer --foreman-proxy-dns true \
                   --foreman-proxy-dns-managed true \
                   --foreman-proxy-dns-interface eth0 \
                   --foreman-proxy-dns-zone example.com \
                   --foreman-proxy-dns-reverse 1.168.192.in-addr.arpa
Subtask 2.3: Configure TFTP Service
Step 1: Install and Configure TFTP
# Install TFTP server
dnf install -y tftp-server xinetd

# Configure TFTP
cat > /etc/xinetd.d/tftp << 'EOF'
service tftp
{
    socket_type     = dgram
    protocol        = udp
    wait            = yes
    user            = root
    server          = /usr/sbin/in.tftpd
    server_args     = -s /var/lib/tftpboot
    disable         = no
    per_source      = 11
    cps             = 100 2
    flags           = IPv4
}
EOF

# Create TFTP directory structure
mkdir -p /var/lib/tftpboot/{boot,pxelinux.cfg}

# Download PXE boot files
dnf install -y syslinux-tftpboot
cp /tftpboot/pxelinux.0 /var/lib/tftpboot/
cp /tftpboot/menu.c32 /var/lib/tftpboot/
cp /tftpboot/chain.c32 /var/lib/tftpboot/

# Set permissions
chmod -R 755 /var/lib/tftpboot
chown -R nobody:nobody /var/lib/tftpboot

# Enable and start services
systemctl enable xinetd
systemctl start xinetd
systemctl status xinetd
Step 2: Configure Satellite TFTP Integration
# Configure TFTP integration
satellite-installer --foreman-proxy-tftp true \
                   --foreman-proxy-tftp-managed true \
                   --foreman-proxy-tftp-servername 192.168.1.20
